# public/legacy is a local-only symlink to the repo root (../..). It exists so the
# dev server can preview the classic atlas, but Next copies public/ into out/ at
# build time and would follow the symlink recursively (out -> public/legacy ->
# repo root -> app -> out -> ...) until the disk fills. Never commit it, and delete
# it before running `next build` locally.
public/legacy